    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86735" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προ-άστιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>suburban,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					721
				</span></i>
			. (The spelling <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αστειο-</span> is
			found in some late Papyri, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				4651.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>, etc., and is freq. in codd., but is proved
			wrong by the metre in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">E., <u>AP</u></span></i>ll.cc.,
			cf. <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστυ</span>
			, also by <u>IG</u>, <u>SIG</u> Il.cc.)</div>
